{"id":"ec0f57f40df6cf7d0b1a7bc59b3249f194958388","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"ec0f57f40df6cf7d0b1a7bc59b3249f194958388","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"Cargo.Bazel.envoy.lock","lines":["@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@"," {","-  \"checksum\": \"9d535d30688f98b4402b9ec935b9491b875a733005af938d4b20b2f2b502b69c\",","+  \"checksum\": \"ad4bb2bb3828b4dc88738d1eef9ac7f6a5a727b839ccc52863f8c5564d87e956\",","   \"conditions\": {","     \"aarch64-apple-darwin\": [","       \"aarch64-apple-darwin\"","@@ -1258,6 +1258,7 @@","         ],","         \"edition\": \"2021\"","       },","+      \"library_target_name\": \"envoy_dynamic_modules_builtin_extensions\",","       \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",","       \"license_ids\": [","         \"Apache-2.0\"","@@ -1265,7 +1266,14 @@","       \"name\": \"envoy-dynamic-modules-builtin-extensions\",","       \"package_url\": \"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy\",","       \"repository\": null,","-      \"targets\": [],","+      \"targets\": [","+        {","+          \"Library\": {","+            \"crate_name\": \"envoy_dynamic_modules_builtin_extensions\",","+            \"crate_root\": \"lib.rs\"","+          }","+        }","+      ],","       \"version\": \"0.1.0\"","     },","     \"envoy-proxy-dynamic-modules-rust-sdk 0.1.0\": {"],"additions":10,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/intro/arch_overview/advanced/dynamic_modules.rst","lines":["@@ -56,6 +56,29 @@ There are a few design goals for the dynamic modules:"," 2. **Ease of Use**: The SDK should provide a high-level API that abstracts the details of the Envoy internals."," 3. **Flexibility**: The dynamic modules should be able to implement any functionality that can be implemented by the built-in C++ extensions without performance penalty. This is work in progress and many features are not yet available."," ","+Built-in Rust modules","+---------------------","+","+Rust dynamic modules linked into the Envoy binary must use ``envoy_rust_static_module`` from","+:repo:`dynamic_modules.bzl <source/extensions/dynamic_modules/dynamic_modules.bzl>`, not","+``rust_static_library``. The macro links the module and its SDK as always-linked Rust libraries","+(rlibs), preserving transitive Rust dependencies so the binary shares one toolchain-provided Rust","+runtime. A Rust staticlib bundles its own copy of that runtime and conflicts with other Rust code,","+such as the wasmtime engine or another built-in module.","+","+The SDK's intentionally empty ``rust_runtime`` staticlib provides the allocator shim and std","+runtime exactly once. It is the only Rust staticlib in the binary; all other Rust code linked","+into Envoy, including engines such as wasmtime, must be rlibs. The macro links this shared","+runtime without applying the module's symbol-prefix transition so Bazel deduplicates it.","+","+The macro's ``module_name`` must match the name passed to the static module loader. It configures","+a separate SDK instance whose exported hooks are named ``<module_name>_envoy_dynamic_module_on_*``.","+The SDK's init macros use the same prefix in the module crate. Hand-written ABI hooks must use","+``#[export_name = envoy_proxy_dynamic_modules_rust_sdk::__export_name!(\"envoy_dynamic_module_on_...\")]``","+instead of ``#[no_mangle]``. Rust handles platform-specific symbol decoration, including the","+leading underscore on macOS. Shared modules and ordinary Cargo SDK builds keep unprefixed hook","+names by default.","+"," HTTP stream timing"," ------------------"," "],"additions":23,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/builtin_extensions/BUILD","lines":["@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@"," load(\"@envoy_rust_crate_index//:defs.bzl\", \"all_crate_deps\")","-load(\"@rules_rust//rust:defs.bzl\", \"rust_clippy\", \"rust_static_library\", \"rustfmt_test\")","+load(\"@rules_rust//rust:defs.bzl\", \"rust_clippy\", \"rustfmt_test\")"," load(\"//bazel:envoy_build_system.bzl\", \"envoy_extension_package\")","-load(\"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules:dynamic_modules.bzl\", \"envoy_dynamic_module_prefix_symbols\")","+load(\"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules:dynamic_modules.bzl\", \"envoy_rust_static_module\")"," "," licenses([\"notice\"])  # Apache 2"," ","@@ -9,37 +9,30 @@ envoy_extension_package()"," "," exports_files([\"Cargo.toml\"])"," ","-rust_static_library(","-    name = \"builtin_extensions_static_lib\",","+envoy_rust_static_module(","+    name = \"hickory_dns_static\",","     srcs = glob([\"*.rs\"]),","     crate_root = \"lib.rs\",","     edition = \"2021\",","-    deps = [","-        \"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust:envoy_proxy_dynamic_modules_rust_sdk\",","-    ] + all_crate_deps(","-        normal = True,","-    ),","-)","-","-envoy_dynamic_module_prefix_symbols(","-    name = \"hickory_dns_static\",","-    archive = \":builtin_extensions_static_lib\",","     module_name = \"hickory_dns_static\",","     visibility = [","         \"//source/extensions/network/dns_resolver/hickory:__pkg__\",","     ],","+    deps = all_crate_deps(","+        normal = True,","+    ),"," )"," "," rustfmt_test(","     name = \"fmt_builtin_extensions\",","     testonly = True,","     tags = [\"nocoverage\"],","-    targets = [\":builtin_extensions_static_lib\"],","+    targets = [\":hickory_dns_static_lib\"],"," )"," "," rust_clippy(","     name = \"clippy_builtin_extensions\",","     testonly = True,","     tags = [\"nocoverage\"],","-    deps = [\":builtin_extensions_static_lib\"],","+    deps = [\":hickory_dns_static_lib\"],"," )"],"additions":9,"deletions":16,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/builtin_extensions/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -19,4 +19,4 @@ url = \"2\""," [lib]"," name = \"envoy_dynamic_modules_builtin_extensions\""," path = \"lib.rs\"","-crate-type = [\"staticlib\"]","+crate-type = [\"rlib\"]"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/dynamic_modules.bzl","lines":["@@ -1,6 +1,76 @@"," \"\"\"Bazel rules for building Envoy dynamic modules.\"\"\""," "," load(\"@rules_cc//cc:defs.bzl\", \"cc_import\")","+load(\"@rules_cc//cc/common:cc_common.bzl\", \"cc_common\")","+load(\"@rules_cc//cc/common:cc_info.bzl\", \"CcInfo\")","+load(\"@rules_rust//rust:defs.bzl\", \"rust_library\")","+","+_SYMBOL_PREFIX = str(Label(\"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust:symbol_prefix\"))","+","+def _symbol_prefix_transition_impl(_settings, attr):","+    return {_SYMBOL_PREFIX: attr.module_name + \"_\"}","+","+_symbol_prefix_transition = transition(","+    implementation = _symbol_prefix_transition_impl,","+    inputs = [],","+    outputs = [_SYMBOL_PREFIX],","+)","+","+def _rust_static_module_impl(ctx):","+    module = ctx.attr.module[0]","+    cc_info = cc_common.merge_cc_infos(","+        cc_infos = [module[CcInfo], ctx.attr._rust_runtime[CcInfo]],","+    )","+    return [cc_info, DefaultInfo(files = module[DefaultInfo].files)]","+","+_rust_static_module = rule(","+    implementation = _rust_static_module_impl,","+    attrs = {","+        \"module\": attr.label(cfg = _symbol_prefix_transition, providers = [CcInfo]),","+        \"module_name\": attr.string(mandatory = True),","+        \"_allowlist_function_transition\": attr.label(","+            default = \"@bazel_tools//tools/allowlists/function_transition_allowlist\",","+        ),","+        \"_rust_runtime\": attr.label(","+            default = Label(\"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust:rust_runtime\"),","+            providers = [CcInfo],","+        ),","+    },","+)","+","+def envoy_rust_static_module(name, module_name, deps = [], tags = [], visibility = None, **kwargs):","+    \"\"\"Builds an in-binary Rust module with its own prefixed SDK.","+","+    The transition configures both the module and its SDK with the same prefix.","+    Both are always-linked rlibs: unlike a Rust staticlib, these do not bundle a","+    private copy of std/compiler_builtins, and retain rules_rust's transitive CcInfo.","+    The SDK's rust_runtime staticlib supplies the allocator shim and std once.","+    It is shared without the prefix transition; all other in-binary Rust code must be rlibs.","+    Rust's export_name handles platform-specific C symbol decoration.","+","+    Args:","+        name: C++-compatible target name. The Rust target is <name>_lib.","+        module_name: Module name used by the static module loader.","+        deps: Rust dependencies, in addition to the SDK.","+        tags: Tags forwarded to both targets.","+        visibility: Visibility of the C++-compatible target.","+        **kwargs: Arguments forwarded to rust_library.","+    \"\"\"","+    rust_library(","+        name = name + \"_lib\",","+        alwayslink = True,","+        deps = [Label(\"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust:envoy_proxy_dynamic_modules_rust_sdk\")] + deps,","+        tags = tags,","+        **kwargs","+    )","+    _rust_static_module(","+        name = name,","+        module = \":\" + name + \"_lib\",","+        module_name = module_name,","+        tags = tags,","+        testonly = kwargs.get(\"testonly\", False),","+        visibility = visibility,","+    )"," "," def envoy_dynamic_module_prefix_symbols(name, module_name, archive, tags = [], **kwargs):","     \"\"\"Renames envoy_dynamic_module_on_* symbols in a pre-built static archive.","@@ -13,8 +83,8 @@ def envoy_dynamic_module_prefix_symbols(name, module_name, archive, tags = [], *","     bazel/exported_symbols.txt, making them available for dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, ...)","     lookup."," ","-    This rule is language-independent: the archive may come from cc_library,","-    rust_static_library, or any other rule that produces a static archive.","+    Use this rule for C/C++ archives. Rust modules must use envoy_rust_static_module","+    instead so they share the toolchain's Rust runtime with other Rust code."," ","     Args:","         name: Bazel target name."],"additions":72,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust/BUILD","lines":["@@ -1,11 +1,13 @@","+load(\"@bazel_skylib//rules:common_settings.bzl\", \"string_flag\")"," load(\"@envoy_rust_crate_index//:defs.bzl\", \"all_crate_deps\", \"crate_deps\")"," load(\"@rules_rust//cargo:defs.bzl\", \"cargo_build_script\")","-load(\"@rules_rust//rust:defs.bzl\", \"rust_library\", \"rust_test\")","+load(\"@rules_rust//rust:defs.bzl\", \"rust_library\", \"rust_static_library\", \"rust_test\")"," load(","     \"//bazel:envoy_build_system.bzl\",","     \"envoy_extension_package\","," )"," load(\"//bazel:toolchains.bzl\", \"LLVM_MAJOR\")","+load(\":symbol_prefix.bzl\", \"symbol_prefix_env\")"," "," licenses([\"notice\"])  # Apache 2"," ","@@ -13,6 +15,31 @@ envoy_extension_package()"," "," exports_files([\"Cargo.toml\"])"," ","+# Provides the Rust allocator shim (__rust_alloc etc) and std runtime exactly","+# once in the final C++ link. All other in-binary Rust code must be rlibs","+# (see envoy_rust_static_module in dynamic_modules.bzl).","+rust_static_library(","+    name = \"rust_runtime\",","+    srcs = [\"runtime.rs\"],","+    edition = \"2021\",","+    visibility = [\"//visibility:public\"],","+)","+","+string_flag(","+    name = \"symbol_prefix\",","+    build_setting_default = \"\",","+)","+","+config_setting(","+    name = \"unprefixed\",","+    flag_values = {\":symbol_prefix\": \"\"},","+)","+","+symbol_prefix_env(","+    name = \"symbol_prefix_env\",","+    prefix = \":symbol_prefix\",","+)","+"," # abi/abi.h is a symlink, which git may check out as a plain text file on Windows."," # Point the build script at the original header instead."," _WINDOWS_ENV = {","@@ -35,6 +62,7 @@ cargo_build_script(","         \"@platforms//os:windows\": _WINDOWS_ENV,","         \"//conditions:default\": {},","     }),","+    build_script_env_files = [\":symbol_prefix_env\"],","     data = [","         \":abi/abi.h\",","     ] + select({","@@ -60,8 +88,16 @@ cargo_build_script("," rust_library(","     name = \"envoy_proxy_dynamic_modules_rust_sdk\",","     srcs = glob([\"src/**/*.rs\"]),","+    # Generated compile data makes rules_rust rebase the crate root into the","+    # configuration's output directory. Its crate hash must differ per prefix,","+    # isolating Rust-mangled factory state as well as the exported C hooks.","+    compile_data = [\":symbol_prefix_env\"],","     edition = \"2021\",","     deps = crate_deps([\"smallvec\"]) + [\":build_script\"],","+    alwayslink = select({","+        \":unprefixed\": False,","+        \"//conditions:default\": True,","+    }),"," )"," "," # Test-only target with mock support enabled via the `mock` feature."],"additions":37,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust/build.rs","lines":["@@ -115,6 +115,24 @@ fn main() {"," ","   let out_path = PathBuf::from(env::var(\"OUT_DIR\").unwrap());"," ","+  // Bake the prefix into the exported macro: env! inside its body would read the","+  // consuming crate's environment instead of the SDK's environment.","+  println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=ENVOY_DYNAMIC_MODULE_SYMBOL_PREFIX\");","+  let prefix = env::var(\"ENVOY_DYNAMIC_MODULE_SYMBOL_PREFIX\").unwrap_or_default();","+  std::fs::write(","+    out_path.join(\"export_name.rs\"),","+    format!(","+      r#\"","+#[doc(hidden)]","+#[macro_export]","+macro_rules! __export_name_impl {{","+  ($name:expr) => {{ concat!({prefix:?}, $name) }};","+}}","+\"#","+    ),","+  )","+  .expect(\"Couldn't write export naming macro\");","+","   let bindings = bindgen::Builder::default()","     .header(abi_header.to_str().unwrap())","     .clang_args(bazel_clang_args())"],"additions":18,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust/runtime.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@","+// Intentionally empty. Building this as a staticlib makes rustc emit the","+// allocator shim and bundle std once for the whole Envoy binary."],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"pat